2026-11-03
- DtIcon: register help, hyperlink and close callbacks through their exact Xt
  callback signatures instead of casting legacy `caddr_t` functions.
- App Builder: emit popup actions and drag-motion handlers with their complete
  Xt contracts, keeping generated applications free of callback casts.
- DtInfo: register the launcher action-completion and timeout routines through
  their native callback types instead of casting a by-value timeout identifier.
- DtSearch: route dtsrcreate's emergency database close through a typed exit
  adapter rather than casting the no-argument database routine.
- App Builder: give project, browser and object translation actions their exact
  `XtActionProc` argument contracts. Resize event handlers and double-click
  timers now implement their Xt callback types directly, without registration
  casts.
- DtSvc: give action translations, timers, prompt handlers, message logging,
  command termination handlers and database converters their exact callback
  and function-table contracts. Registrations no longer cast functions with
  incompatible types.
- DtSearch: route database-close and shared-memory cleanup through typed exit
  adapters instead of storing incompatible functions in exit-hook slots. Text
  parser reader callbacks now implement their shared opaque-argument contract
  directly.
