  signatures, including argument lists and base-class widget parameters.
- DtWidget: align Editor, Icon, SpinBox and TitleBox class methods, action
  tables, synthetic-resource hooks and gadget dispatch with their framework
  callback types.
- DtInfo: preprocess the aggregate message input from the shadow build
  directory where it is generated, and materialize the preprocessor stream
  before running the catalog converter. A missing generated input now fails
  the build instead of being masked by a successful downstream pipeline, and
  the final catalog is replaced atomically only after both stages succeed.
- build: keep Autoconf's Flex link probe valid under strict C23 by selecting
  the POSIX declaration level required by generated scanners. Configure now
  checks the usable `LEX` result rather than merely the discovered executable,
  so a missing or unusable lexer is reported before a clean DtMmdb build can
  silently run a no-op generator and fail on an absent generated source.
